{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1372761-nerds-compact","id":1372761,"title":"Nerds Compact","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-04T11:14:42-08:00","id":1372761,"title":"Nerds Compact","content":"Part of joke, but part of the legit idea, years ago I devised basic premise of new Compact - group of hunters that were nerds immersed in popculture, mainly (old) <b>World of Darkness</b> books. Yes, in <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> world. Imagine this - larpers for <b>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</b> found out Uratha are real, but they work not according the rules in their favorite gamebooks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Or that mages are totally different than those shown in <b>Ascension</b>. It got very Null Mysteriis vibe, in what characters have very internalized world view on monsters that is partially wrong.<br /> <br /> I just need good name ( my nemesis! ), and new group write itself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T14:02:25-08:00","id":1372815,"title":"","content":"Good guy needs vs jerk jocks<br /> The jocks are the supernatur","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T22:01:58-08:00","id":1372898,"title":"","content":"Name came literally to me in the dream tonight. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I end write-up later today. For now, enjoy base idea.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>DICE</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Dedicated Individuals Contra Enemies</b><br /> It started with a game. You were in collage, invited to this weird party. Friend of the friend of the friend was doing this impersonation game in the campus bar. You know, like Cludeo, Mafia or shit. Only in this you were assumed to BE a werewolf. Or witch. Or vampire. They called it <b><i>World of Darkness</i></b>. You loved it so much, you still play twenty years later on other weekend and hunt monsters on other Saturday nights.<br /> <br /> In the 90s popular were games from <b>World of Darkness</b> franchise, <b>WoD </b>in short. One of major RPG lines, it wa series of system about iconic popculture monsters \u2013 <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b>, <b>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</b>, <b>Mage: the Ascension</b> and a dozen of others, less known monsters games. They get much popularity in goth and nerd subcultures of those times, being mildly successful. They were easy to immerse as the setting pointing to \u2018our world only darker\u2019. There were also many Live Action Roleplaying ( LARP ) clubs of those games around the world.<br /> <br /> But in few years it ended, when sells were too low. Some more dedicated fans said it was government covering up for monsters. Others said that were monsters itself taking care of those that share truth to much. Most simply understand that RPG industry is running partially on bankruptcy level of low incomes. Well, <b>WoD </b>simply didn\u2019t make it.<br /> <br /> Only it did. DICE was one of the LARP clubs in California. It was mid 90s, <b>WoD </b>was rather strong in fandom and it seemed that everyone is playing it. On one of this Saturday nights in campus woods it was shown that everyone \u2013 and <i>everything</i> \u2013 is really playing it. There was unfortunate combat accident. Normally local Storyteller simply choose game cards or dices or shit like this to resolve the fight. Only this time one player attacked other, for reals - and it was vampire goth chick. Somehow, DICE members instead of running, used all they game lore and killed it. They swear not to tell anybody about it and tried to disband game club. But when each member was attacked in coming weeks \u2013 they banded once more and become real hunters.<br /> <br /> They started DICE forum, where rest of Internet assumed it\u2019s just another RPG fandom sites. In reality, DICE members are testing waters and still look for the players that really got attacked in their past. As popularity of <b>WoD</b> franchise decreases, members started to look in other fandoms also, adding a bit of \u2018knight errant\u2019 and \u2018s-f crazes\u2019 types to their Compact. In early 2000\u2019s they even invited video game cRPG crowd, with popularity of those great single player and then MMORPG games, all about immersion in the role. Now, two decades later, DICE is multi-nerd group of hunters. They even prepare convention next month. Come to join?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Enemy</b></span><br /> Monsters are real \u2013 and they are jerks. We have all the lore we need in our<b> WoD</b> books. Twenty years later, they are now unrealistic expensive on Ebay and other auction sites \u2013 but maybe you were lucky and got your older sister or fathers corebook set. Other games are\u2026 not so much useful. Very rarely we see a dragon on the sky \u2013 but it <i>do</i> happen. Still, RPG players are surprisingly versed in various occult lore. Just ask any one of them about ingredients for they favourite spell or how to kill the werewolf. DICE members maybe somehow polluted by the <b>WoD</b> lore too much and make mistakes by it \u2013 but anyone of them is real fountain of hunter knowledge when around you. And they just like to talk on nerd stuff, with passion.<br /> <br /> With nerd stigma, came a term for enemy \u2013 jerks. DICE needed metaphor for monsters. Looking over they cultural roots, they devised that bullies and jerks from their high school pasts will be great ideas to cover real monsters existence in conversations. And it stayed that way to this day.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Hunters</b><br /> <br /> <b>Factions</b></span><br /> As any larger Compact, DICE is divided into smaller cliques. They are called \u2018fandoms\u2019 and show from where you take your lore \u2013 and where finally is your heart. They help learn you the new and perfect old Skills you need on the hunt.<br /> <br /> <b>WoDers</b>, known also as <i>Old Guard</i>, are veterans of the group. They were playing <b>WoD</b> games with passion and often understand supernatural beings by the eyes of the gamelines. It sometimes helps, sometimes hinders. And they look just like they are from another century. They fandom Skills are Occult and Academics.<br /> <br /> <b><i>New Guard</i></b> are fandom coming from other tabletop RPG worlds. Varied in their take, they point WoDers that real lore is hidden in all those fantasy and S-F games, also. Devising parallels between D&amp;D vampires and Kindred of \u2018real world\u2019 is ambitious task \u2013 but they take it. They fandom Skills are Academics and Science.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Wiz-Kids </i></b>are the video games nerds. Analyzing myriad mythos of popular franchise, with really made up worlds, made them not very useful to proper hunt. Or at least it\u2019s WoDers take. Wiz-Kids point that real world monsters are not putted in neat boxes \u2013 and being open to really bizzare concepts can open you to the lore you need. Besides, they work awesomely as tech guys. They fandom Skills are Academics and Computers.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Status</b></span><br /> Working somehow similar to Null Mysteriis, members of DICE get status by confronting their fandom lore with realities of hunt \u2013 and preparing new advises and lore pieces for next generations of \u2018players\u2019.<br /> <br /> \u2022 You\u2019ve been playing RPG or video games most of your life. You see a marks of vampire, trail of dragon or even alien invasion from afar. Get free dot in Occult just by joining to the group that said you were right all along.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Your hobby is your obsession \u2013 and it\u2019s showing you the way for real knowledge. You get <i>Encyclopedic Knowledge</i> Merit for free, related to the lore of fandom you mostly adhere to.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Your are living embodiment of your fandom lore \u2013 and becoming like living persona of it. You get four dots in <i>Professional Training</i> Merit based on your fandom Skills as Asset Skills. If you already have them, use Sanctify of Merits. If you have <i>Professional Training </i> in one of those Skills, get the <i>Training </i>for the other with added next Assets Skill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-05-2020, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T11:09:29-08:00","id":1373009,"title":"","content":"So I must say I <i>really</i> liked how DICE come to being, in the end. As random idea I got, take more like joke, I did not thought with now rules I can easily mold so much 'passion nerds as hunters' characters. Merits in Status bonuses glues greatly to those larger than life hunters ideas. And, generally, Compact seems to work with <b>HtV</b> setting as it is. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T11:15:44-08:00","id":1373011,"title":"","content":"As inspiration for this group - <i>Charlie Bradbury</i> from <b>Supernatural </b>TV series! She would clearly be from Wiz-Kidz in Compact. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Hh5yCLXOU_Y\" data-code=\"Hh5yCLXOU_Y\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Hh5yCLXOU_Y/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","